# The game's share of the VPS: the compose files put every container of theirs (the server, Caddy or the
# Cloudflare Tunnel's cloudflared and its namespace) into this slice (cgroup_parent), and the slice gets at most
# CPUQuota of the CPU between them, so the rest of the VPS always keeps the remainder whatever the players do.
# 1500 % is 15 of 16 vCPU, 1 left for the rest (nfsu2.xyz: 11.8 of 12.8 taken at 4,300 players, 2026-10-23; the rest
# used about half a vCPU at 5,857, 2026-10-30, when 14 became 15 for 6500 places; 7000 and then 8000 since 2026-10-31, 12000 since 2026-11-01); for another VPS, its vCPUs less
# what the rest needs, x 100.  The server and cloudflared share it as
# their load goes, and the server reads what the slice uses (compose.yml's `cgroup: host`): over 85 % of the quota
# its free-roam hub gives players fewer friends, which costs cloudflared less too; at the quota they are slowed down,
# never the rest of the VPS.
#   cp web/deploy/nfsu2.slice /etc/systemd/system/ && systemctl daemon-reload
# then recreate the containers (docker compose up -d --force-recreate).  Without the file the containers still
# start, in a slice systemd makes for them with no limit.  Needs Docker's systemd cgroup driver (docker info:
# "Cgroup Driver: systemd", the default with cgroup v2).
[Unit]
Description=NFS Underground 2 in the browser: its containers' share of the CPU

[Slice]
CPUAccounting=yes
CPUQuota=1500%
